[al:新概念英语第三册]
[ti:28. A Pound Too Dear]
[00:00.380] Passage 28. | 第28篇
[00:02.135] A pound too dear. | 一英镑太贵了
[00:04.950] Small boats loaded with wares | 载满货品的小船
[00:07.760] sped to the great liner as she was entering the harbor. | 快速驶向正在进港的这艘大型客轮。
[00:10.770] Before she had anchored, | 她还没抛锚，
[00:12.525] the men from the boats had climbed on board, | 船上的人就爬上了客轮，
[00:15.080] and the decks were soon covered with colorful rugs from Persia, | 甲板上很快就摆满了来自波斯的五颜六色的地毯、
[00:18.605] silks from India, | 印度的丝绸、
[00:19.950] copper coffee pots, | 铜质咖啡壶
[00:21.250] and beautiful handmade silverware. | 以及精美的手工银器。
[00:23.655] It was difficult not to be tempted. | 很难不心动。
[00:26.195] Many of the tourists on board had begun bargaining with the tradesmen. | 船上很多游客都和商人讨价还价起来。
[00:30.115] But I decided not to buy anything | 但我决定什么也不买，
[00:32.555] until I had disembarked. | 直到我下了船。
[00:34.740] I had no sooner got off the ship | 我刚下船，
[00:37.215] than I was assailed by a man who wanted to sell me a diamond ring. | 就被一个想卖我一枚钻戒的男人缠住了。
[00:41.240] I had no intention of buying one, | 我本来不打算买，
[00:43.480] but I could not conceal the fact that I was impressed | 但我无法掩饰我对钻石大小的印象之深。
[00:48.185] Some of them were as big as marbles. | 其中一些钻石大如弹珠。
[00:50.785] The man went to great lengths to prove | 这人竭力证明
[00:53.363] that the diamonds were real. | 这些钻石是真的。
[00:54.985] As we were walking past a shop, | 我们路过一家商店时，
[00:57.125] he held a diamond firmly against the window | 他把一颗钻石紧紧地按在窗户上，
[00:59.800] and it made a deep impression in the glass. | 在玻璃上留下了一个深深的印记。
[01:02.300] It took me over half an hour to get rid of him. | 我花了半个多小时才摆脱了他。
[01:05.390] The next man to approach me | 接下来找我的人
[01:07.835] was selling expensive pens and watches. | 卖的是昂贵的钢笔和手表。
[01:10.725] I examined one of the pens closely. | 我仔细检查了一支钢笔。
[01:13.200] It certainly looked genuine. | 它看起来确实是真的。
[01:15.415] At the base of the gold cap, | 在金笔帽的底部，
[01:17.435] the words, | 刻着
[01:18.420] made in the USA, | “美国制造”
[01:20.105] had been neatly inscribed. | 字样。
[01:22.425] The man said that the pen was worth ten pounds, | 那人说这支钢笔值10英镑，
[01:25.965] but as a special favour, | 但作为特别优惠，
[01:27.635] he would let me have it for eight pounds. | 他会以8英镑的价格卖给我。
[01:30.200] I shook my head | 我摇了摇头，
[01:31.680] and held up a finger indicating | 举起一根手指表示
[01:33.565] that I was willing to pay a pound. | 我愿意付一英镑。
[01:35.740] Gesticulating wildly, | 那人疯狂地打着手势，
[01:37.675] the man acted as if he found my offer outrageous. | 表现得好像我的报价令人发指。
[01:40.825] But he eventually reduced the price to three pounds. | 但他最终把价格降到了三英镑。
[01:44.055] Shrugging my shoulders, | 我耸了耸肩，
[01:45.690] I began to walk away, | 开始走开，
[01:47.020] when a moment later, | 没过一会儿，
[01:48.290] he ran after me | 他追上我，
[01:49.400] and thrust the pen into my hands. | 把钢笔塞到我手里。
[01:51.615] Though he kept throwing up his arms in despair, | 尽管他绝望地不停挥舞着手臂，
[01:54.445] he readily accepted the pound I gave him. | 他还是欣然接受了我给他的一英镑。
[01:57.395] I felt especially pleased with my wonderful bargain | 我对我的这笔美妙交易感到特别满意，
[02:01.180] until I got back to the ship. | 直到我回到船上。
[02:03.515] No matter how hard I tried, | 无论我怎么努力，
[02:06.005] it was impossible to fill this beautiful pen with ink. | 都无法把墨水灌满这支漂亮的钢笔。
[02:09.505] And to this day, | 直到今天，
[02:11.035] it has never written a single word. | 它也从未写过一个字。